VeridianOS: drop the process plugins' stale translation domain

processcore/CMakeLists.txt defines TRANSLATION_DOMAIN as "processcore";
its plugins directory added "ksysguard_plugins_process" on top, so the
plugins were compiled with both (GCC: "'TRANSLATION_DOMAIN' redefined")
and took whichever came last on the command line. Since upstream commit
2c893a09 the plugins' strings are extracted into the processcore catalog
and ksysguard_plugins_process no longer exists, so the stale definition
is removed and the plugins use the inherited one. (Prepared for
upstream, invent.kde.org/plasma/libksysguard.)

--- a/processcore/plugins/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/processcore/plugins/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,3 @@
-add_definitions(-DTRANSLATION_DOMAIN=\"ksysguard_plugins_process\")
 if (BUILD_NETWORK_PLUGIN)
     add_subdirectory(network)
 endif()
